cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this corpus, cite the release you actually built against, by its
  tag. The tag is a complete byte pin: data/corpus is git-tracked, so the tag
  fixes every served passage. data/corpus_release.json carries that release's
  id, per-source counts and quality caveats; data/corpus_catalog.tsv carries one
  row per work with its own sha256. There is no DOI for this corpus - cite the
  tag and the repository.
title: Open Greek Corpus
abstract: >-
  An open corpus of ancient Greek: openly-licensed digital editions where they
  exist, our own OCR of public-domain editions where they do not, with the goal
  of a free counterpart to the subscription corpora. Text is served as one
  locus-keyed JSONL file per work, with a per-work catalog, an id layer
  (opaque work and author ids crosswalked to CTS/TLG, Wikidata, VIAF/GND/ISNI),
  and per-lemma and per-work frequency tables. Part of the corpus is OCR of
  pre-1930 public-domain editions and is corrected to varying degrees, so quality
  is uneven by design and is published per work rather than averaged away.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Riordan
    given-names: Francisco
repository-code: "https://github.com/open-greek/open-greek-corpus"
version: corpus-2026-08-04
date-released: "2026-08-04"
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
keywords:
  - ancient Greek
  - Greek literature
  - corpus linguistics
  - digital classics
  - TEI
  - OCR
  - CTS
# Licensing is not uniform, and the single `license` field above cannot say so.
# The aggregate is CC BY-SA 4.0, because the bulk of it is CC BY-SA 4.0 editions
# redistributed under the same terms; our own OCR of public-domain editions is
# ADDITIONALLY available under CC BY 4.0; the derived statistical tables (lemma
# frequency, coverage counts) are facts and carry no copyright. No
# non-commercial (CC BY-NC-SA) text is included. LICENSE states this in full,
# and each work's own source and license are in data/coverage.json and
# data/corpus_catalog.tsv.
#
# The references below are the aggregated corpora whose licenses require
# attribution when you redistribute the text. Attribution is also due to the
# individual editors recorded per work in data/coverage.json.
references:
  - type: data
    title: First1KGreek
    authors:
      - name: Open Greek and Latin
    license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
    url: "https://github.com/OpenGreekAndLatin/First1KGreek"
    notes: First-millennium Greek TEI editions; the bulk of the aggregated text.
  - type: data
    title: canonical-greekLit
    authors:
      - name: Perseus Digital Library
    license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
    url: "https://github.com/PerseusDL/canonical-greekLit"
    notes: The classical canon, TEI; the other bulk source.
  - type: data
    title: Galenus Verbatim
    authors:
      - name: "Galenus Verbatim (Sorbonne Universite)"
    license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
    url: "https://github.com/galenus-verbatim/galenus_cts"
    notes: Galen and pseudo-Galen TEI.
  - type: data
    title: "Patrologia Graeca (OCR)"
    authors:
      - name: Calfa
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    url: "https://github.com/calfa-co/Patrologia-Graeca"
    notes: CC-BY OCR of the public-domain Migne Patrologia Graeca.
  - type: data
    title: Patristic Text Archive
    authors:
      - name: "Berlin-Brandenburgische Akademie der Wissenschaften"
    license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
    url: "https://github.com/PatristicTextArchive/pta_data"
    notes: >-
      Critical patristic TEI; licensed per file (CC BY-SA or CC BY), and the one
      CC BY-NC-SA file is excluded rather than served.
  - type: data
    title: "Digital Fragmenta Historicorum Graecorum"
    authors:
      - name: "DFHG Project, Universitat Leipzig"
    license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
    url: "https://www.dfhg-project.org"
    notes: Mueller's Fragmenta Historicorum Graecorum vols 1-5, corrected transcription.
  - type: data
    title: Sharing Ancient Wisdoms
    authors:
      - name: "SAWS Project"
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    doi: 10.18742/28259054.v1
    url: "https://ancientwisdoms.ac.uk"
    notes: >-
      Born-digital editions and diplomatic transcriptions; the 2025 KCL figshare
      deposit, which supersedes the project's 2013 in-file CC BY-NC-SA notices.
  - type: data
    title: "GLAUx: the Greek Language Automated"
    authors:
      - name: Alek Keersmaekers
    license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
    url: "https://github.com/alekkeersmaekers/glaux"
    notes: >-
      Source of the served text of Julius Pollux, Onomasticon, and of the Bekker
      concordance milestones.
  - type: data
    title: Greek Wikisource
    authors:
      - name: Greek Wikisource contributors
    license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
    url: "https://el.wikisource.org"
    notes: >-
      Proofread transcriptions of public-domain editions; the base texts are
      public domain, the contributor transcription layer is CC BY-SA 4.0.
  - type: data
    title: "Opera Graeca Adnotata (v0.2.0)"
    authors:
      - family-names: Celano
        given-names: "Giuseppe G. A."
    license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.14206061
    year: 2024
    notes: >-
      Metadata only, no text: per-work composition dating and the PTA/TLG
      duplicate map. Pinned by version DOI in sources/oga/manifest.json.
